body:
CSS uses selectors to choose elements and declarations to style them. Add the following inside a style element in your HTML page.
CODE:body { background: #100d19; color: white; }
h1 { color: #a67aff; }
Practice: change the heading colour and add padding to the body.

Variables store values. Use const for a value you will not reassign and let for a value that can change.
CODE:const learner = 'Bright';
let lessonsCompleted = 0;
console.log(learner);
Practice: run this in your browser developer console.

Functions group instructions so you can reuse them.
CODE:function greet(name) {
  return 'Welcome, ' + name;
}
console.log(greet('Bright'));
Practice: call the function with your own name.

Events let your page react to user actions.
CODE:const button = document.querySelector('button');
button.addEventListener('click', () => {
  button.textContent = 'Clicked!';
});
Practice: add a button to your HTML page and connect this script.
